  "section_notes": "Final S1 is strict: all thermal incidents reportable, serious within 24h and others within 5 business days, with customer notice in 24h for ongoing hazards. S2 is the main weakened section: 55°C testing and a 5% failure-rate threshold remain, but exceeding it triggers corrective action and regulator review rather than an automatic sales stop, and per-model results go to customers/regulators but not the public. S3/S4/S5 land in acceptable/safe territory: 6-year retrofit with alternative, built-in suppression at 36 months, and a mandatory 8/100k recall with immediate notices but no serious-injury clause."
